    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6-a8">

                <pb facs="0126" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg18"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Schlessing to Mr. Grant.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1893-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic">May 22,
                                1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Very respectfully referring to our personal
                    interview of yesterday in respect to John Benich, a naturalized citizen of the
                    United States, having been seized by the imperial and royal authorities of
                    Austria-Hungary in order to make him perform military duty, I have the honor to
                    herein inclose the following three communications, as specified at foot of this,
                    from the consular agency at Fiume, and bearing on that subject; inclosure No. 3
                    also, containing the request of the consular agent, Mr. Gelletich, that the
                    Hungarian authorities, and especially the Croatian judge of Novi, might be
                    caused to recognize Mr. Gelletich’s authority as U. S. consular agent.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Schlessing</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Deputy Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
